      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:02:31.771Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:02:31.771Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7chivqwa06x4uon9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1094,
      "y": 410,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "text": "≈ 2.77 V when armed\n12 V × 3 / (10 + 3)",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:02:31.771Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:02:31.771Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7chivqg95e7wkrgh8",
      "type": "line",
      "x": 700,
      "y": 188,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "points": [
        [
          0,
          0
        ],
        [
          130,
          0
        ]
      ],
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:02:31.771Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:02:31.771Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7chivqcssnx38v4wu",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 540,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "text": "The 3 kΩ is the lower leg of the divider and it MUST\nland on the junction. Omit it and the pin STILL READS\nHIGH: it sees 12 V through 10 kΩ with the Zener as the\nonly thing between the rail and a 3.3 V input, passing\n~0.9 mA continuously. It \"works\" until the Zener dies.\nThat is what makes the omission dangerous rather than\nmerely wrong.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:02:31.771Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:02:31.771Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7chivqw0ufwm0hz5q",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 470,
      "y": 540,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "text": "Meter every resistor before soldering. An\nundersized lower leg drops the junction below\nV_IH and the Pi never reads armed.\n\n100 nF debounces the switch. The 10 kΩ limits\ncurrent from the 12 V rail.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:02:31.771Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:02:31.771Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7chivqzr0b418pos9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 900,
      "y": 540,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "text": "BZX55C3V3 — cathode (the banded end) at the junction,\nanode to GND. Fitted backwards it is a forward-biased\ndiode pinning the junction near 0.7 V, so the Pi can\nnever read armed. Fail-safe, but silent and baffling.\nConfirm the band with a multimeter diode test.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:02:31.771Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:02:31.771Z",
      "version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ms7chivqfo3sux7izs",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 726,
      "strokeColor": "#e8590c",
      "text": "E-STOP → GPIO 25   (active LOW, fail-safe)",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-30T10:02:31.771Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T10:02:31.771Z",
      "version": 1
    },
